# Nipomo SC Instagram Analytics MCP Server

## What This Is

A local MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that connects to the Meta Graph API, giving Claude Code on-demand access to @nipomo.soccer's Instagram analytics. It pulls post-level performance data, follower growth, audience demographics, and content comparisons -- then surfaces actionable recommendations for what to post next, tied to the club's content pillars and social media plan.

## Core Value

Claude can pull real Instagram performance data during any conversation and recommend what content to create next based on what's actually working.

## Requirements

### Validated

(None yet -- ship to validate)

### Active

- [ ] MCP server connects to Meta Graph API with Instagram Business account credentials
- [ ] Pull post-level metrics: reach, impressions, engagement rate, saves, shares per post/reel
- [ ] Pull follower growth data over configurable time windows
- [ ] Pull audience demographics: age ranges, geographic locations
- [ ] Compare performance across content pillars (identity, program info, community, social proof)
- [ ] Identify top-performing content by engagement metrics
- [ ] Surface optimal posting times based on audience activity data
- [ ] Benchmark against competitor accounts (local SLO County/Central Coast clubs + similar-sized youth sports accounts)
- [ ] Generate "what to post next" recommendations based on performance gaps and content calendar
- [ ] Run locally on Mac as an MCP server accessible to Claude Code

### Out of Scope

- Comment reading/replying -- focus on analytics only for v1
- DM management -- requires separate Meta app review with messaging permissions
- Content publishing/scheduling -- use existing tools (Ashley's workflow)
- Cloud hosting -- local-only for now, though architecture should not preclude future migration
- Cross-platform analytics (Facebook, TikTok) -- Instagram only for v1

## Context

- @nipomo.soccer is the club's Instagram account, run by Johnny (strategy, captions) and Ashley (graphics, scheduling)
- The account follows a 5-week social media plan with defined content pillars and posting ratios
- Current registration push for RISE Spring Development League (55/200 target as of March 15)
- The club needs data-driven content decisions, not just gut feel
- Meta Graph API requires a Meta Developer App and Instagram Business/Creator account token
- MCP servers integrate natively with Claude Code via configuration

## Constraints

- **API**: Meta Graph API rate limits (200 calls/user/hour for most endpoints)
- **Auth**: Requires Meta Developer App approval and long-lived access token management
- **Competitor data**: Meta API only exposes public metrics for business accounts via Instagram Basic Display API / scraping is against TOS -- competitor benchmarking limited to publicly available data
- **Local runtime**: Must run as a local process on macOS, started alongside Claude Code sessions
- **Token refresh**: Meta tokens expire; server must handle token refresh or alert when expired

## Key Decisions

| Decision | Rationale | Outcome |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| Local MCP server (not cloud) | Simplest setup, no hosting cost, sufficient for on-demand use | -- Pending |
| No comment/DM features in v1 | Keeps scope tight, avoids Meta messaging permissions review | -- Pending |
| Node.js runtime | MCP SDK has first-class TypeScript/Node support | -- Pending |
| Competitor benchmarking via public data only | Meta TOS prohibits scraping; API access to others' accounts is limited | -- Pending |

